WEBVTT

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.180
The current routine goes like this.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.230
The new routine goes like this.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:20.070
It ain't just the lift, either.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:24.290
The moves between the first and 
third tumbling passes are different.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.070
It's an overall increase in difficulty.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:30.170
Especially Misato-kun's lift.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:34.980
A backward leap will require a stronger
 foundation and more coordination.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.460
Good thing we've got our Safe and Trusty Ace!

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:58.170
Wha?! He blew me off!

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.400
I know it's annoying, Misato, but...

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.190
You can't just leave a man hangin'.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.540
At least humor our obnoxious friend.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.450
"Obnoxious friend"?

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:09.290
Oh, sorry.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.900
Well, let's get started.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.060
Yes, sir!

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:45.010
<b><i>Backflip!!</i></b>

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:48.280
Well, let's try the lift.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.520
Sir!

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.620
What's up, Misato?

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.770
I'm sorry. I messed up the timing.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.310
I'd like to try it again.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:34.000
Sure.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:04.630
I'm sorry.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:07.820
What's up? You off your game?

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.720
Er, no. Let's give it another try.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:13.450
No, I think we should give it a rest.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:15.380
Please let me try again.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.340
We have plenty of time. 
There's no need to rush.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:20.210
But...

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:22.240
I don't want you injuring yourself.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:28.850
Yes, sir.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.010
Comin' in!

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:39.550
I'm worried about our ace...

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:42.090
What's he so afraid of?

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.330
I wonder.

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:46.140
I've never seen him like this before.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:38.940
Misato...

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:43.940
So you don't trust us as 
your foundation or somethin'?

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:47.950
Hey, Watari.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.350
No... I'm sorry.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.700
That's it for morning practice.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.880
We'll pick up after classes.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.000
S-Sir!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.220
Yah!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.220
Yes, sir!

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:00.100
Misato-kun!

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:03.470
What's wrong?

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:05.010
Nothing.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.040
Do you feel ill—

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:07.150
I'm fine.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:19.670
Misato bailed?

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:20.770
Yes.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:23.940
I can't find him anywhere on campus.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:29.660
I'm back.

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:37.110
Ryo-chan? What's up?

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:46.770
I heard Misato-kun stayed home today...

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:51.060
W-Was it because of what I said to him?!

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:55.600
I mean... who skips school 
'cause they can't handle a lift?

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:00.520
I'm going to stop by his house.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.030
Then I'll come with.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:03.190
That's okay.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:06.400
Let's go, Futaba-kun.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.990
You've been wanting to talk 
to him, haven't you?

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:13.390
Yes!

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.910
<b>Hirose

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:23.170
Hirose?

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:27.040
I guess they're not home.

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:28.590
Excuse me...

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:30.840
Can I help you?

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:39.530
I know that face from somewhere...

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:41.690
But where?

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:42.960
Um...

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:46.880
I'm the men's rhythmic gymnastics
 coach at Ao High.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:49.500
Oh, you're Coach Shida!

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.930
I appreciate you looking after Ryo-chan.

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:52.990
Oh, don't mention it.

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:56.470
I'm his aunt, Sakiko Hirose.

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:57.910
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.520
His aunt?

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:04.980
Huh? Where is it again?

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:07.040
I'll just be a minute!

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:11.800
The tea, the tea...

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:13.130
Don't go out of your way.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:18.980
I'm just hopeless around the house...

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:23.310
<i>Teamwork is important 
in men's rhythmic gymnastics.</i>

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:25.770
<i>So the boys live in a dorm together.</i>

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.980
<i>I really need to go home in the evenings.</i>

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:33.140
He shows up last night and says,

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:36.200
"You really are helpless without me."

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.870
Okay, that's a bad impression.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.470
Ah, there it is!

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:50.060
Did something happen 
with Ryo-chan and the team?

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:53.340
It's nothing to worry about.

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.140
Our lift...

00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:01.030
I mean, he and I are working 
on a move together.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.020
But it's not going well.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:05.400
A lift?

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.090
Does that mean anything to you?

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:13.530
It was... his second year 
of junior high, I think.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:23.550
He's hesitant to do lifts, then?

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:25.720
But he's never had trouble before...

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:30.680
The new lift we're trying means trusting
 your teammates to get the timing right.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:35.150
I see.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:37.510
So he hasn't changed.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:51.750
Ryo-chan's mother was my big sister.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:54.640
His parents are...

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:12.110
His junior high coach said the same thing.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:15.300
He's very diligent and cares deeply 
about his teammates,

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:18.600
but he seems to keep them at arm's length.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:19.880
He does?

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:21.100
Yes.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.770
Ever since he was a child, 
he's kind of had a thing

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:27.150
about being as independent as possible.

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:30.970
I think it's because he 
doesn't want to burden me.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:36.190
So it's not that he doesn't 
trust his friends.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:40.590
It's more like... he just can't fully 
put himself in their hands.

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:45.370
Like he feels a responsibility 
to handle everything himself.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:51.670
I see.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.800
I'm sure I know your face from somewhere...

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.550
Here!

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:07.900
Scary! Who's that?

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:10.510
He looks so mean.

00:11:10.510 --> 00:11:14.020
Although he does seem familiar...

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:18.050
It's me.

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:20.620
That's me when I was younger.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:21.590
How embarrassing.

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:22.050
What?!

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:23.400
I knew it!

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:26.210
I knew I'd seen you somewhere before.

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:30.120
There was a period when Ryo-chan 
was really in the dumps.

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:33.700
But when he found some
 men's rhythmic gymnastics videos,

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:37.410
he said, "I want to be like this guy. 
I want to be a cool jumper like him."

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:38.710
And then he started trying.

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:46.270
Then the reason he came to Ao High is...

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:51.980
<b>Hirose

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:51.980
Sorry to impose.

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:54.180
When Misato-kun returns...

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:56.400
Of course. I'll call you first thing.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:02.640
Oh, Ryo-chan.

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:05.470
Coach... Futaba...

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:07.120
Welcome home, Misato-kun.

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:12.770
I'm heading back.

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:14.510
I'll leave you two alone to talk.

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:16.080
Okay.

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:29.900
Misato-kun!

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:31.620
I know, all right?

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.380
It's my weakness.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:38.150
I'm socially awkward.

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:42.110
I don't know how to build
 trusting relationships.

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:48.740
No... I just don't know how to trust anyone.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:52.880
I came to the dorm in hopes
 of getting over that.

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:55.350
It's okay, though.

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:58.380
I spent the day thinking, 
and I'm ready to do things right.

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:00.090
Futaba.

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.570
I'm going to trust you all.

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:04.470
You're going to trust us?

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:07.070
Yeah. I've made up my mind.

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:09.720
I'm going to believe in you
 and the captain more.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.560
So you don't have to worry.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:16.230
I'm going home now.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:21.110
Wait! That doesn't sound right!

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:25.110
What doesn't?

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:27.820
Deciding that <i>you're</i>
 going to believe in <i>us</i>...

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:31.190
That's just you taking on 
everything yourself again!

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:36.600
That's not how this works! 
That's not even close to real trust!

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.510
Then what exactly am I supposed to do?

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:48.960
Huh? W-Well...

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:56.380
B-Be needy?

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:59.270
Yeah, that's it! You have to be needy!

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.330
What?

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:04.730
Being part of a team means you
need other people! You need our help!

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:06.900
So <i>need</i> us already!

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:10.160
B-But I don't know how to be needy...

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.410
I can't do everything for you alone,

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:15.410
but you've got the rest of the team 
and our coach, too!

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:18.430
Okay, let's get back and get needy!

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:20.670
N-No, I still don't know how...

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.710
Come on! Let's get going!

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:24.880
Wait, Futaba!

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:31.390
I'm sorry for worrying you all.

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:38.520
I... I'm...

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:41.270
It's fine. You don't hafta tell us
if you don't wanna.

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:45.670
Everyone's got somethin' or other
 they're shy about.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:47.800
Except for maybe you, Captain.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:48.530
Whazzat?!

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:51.150
Sometimes a man just needs a day off.

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:54.490
I'm sorry about what I said!

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:57.600
Er... that really had nothing to do with it.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:00.580
Anyway, let's make this a fresh start.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:01.480
Let's.

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:06.260
All right.

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:07.210
Yeah!

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.090
On that note...

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:13.390
Be needy. <i>Be needy!</i>

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:21.520
I... I have a favor to ask of you all.

00:15:21.890 --> 00:15:25.350
I really want to get this move right!

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:28.280
So... please...

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:31.780
Please let me take all the practice I need!

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:33.030
Please!

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:38.820
Misato.

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:41.300
How could we ever refuse

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:43.500
such a request from our Returning Ace?

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:45.360
Don't call me that.

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:48.300
Gosh, gotta love that Pavlovian response!

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:51.010
You're not soaring under your own power.

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:53.300
You need us to set you flyin'!

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:54.180
That's right.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:59.460
For group competitions, you really need 
to bond with and understand your teammates.

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:01.510
Yeah, you said it!

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:02.440
Indeed.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:04.700
Which means...

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:06.440
Tan Tan!

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.860
Sasakama!

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:09.400
Yakuza!

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:11.280
Greenery!

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:43.520
Tan-Sasa-Za-Nery! Tan-Sasa-Za-Nery!

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:21.040
When did they practice that?

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.000
It's so coordinated...

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.360
Behold the bonds of the Ao High 
men's rhythmic gymnastics team!

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:29.830
Come on, you two! Join us!

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:31.510
Shotaro! Misato!

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:33.260
I flat-out refuse.

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:35.240
Let's do it, Misato-kun!

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:37.390
This is part of being needy.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:40.350
It can't possibly be...

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:43.520
I mean, I'm not eager to join in either...

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:45.270
I heard that, Shotaro!

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:47.470
S-Sorry!

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:49.930
To be honest,
 I'm not thrilled about this myself.

00:16:49.930 --> 00:16:51.930
Tsukidate, you traitor!

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:54.530
S'right! S'right!

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:02.190
I feel so relaxed...

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:19.270
Shotaro.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:22.290
Yeah?

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:27.350
I plan to get a job 
straight out of high school.

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:32.020
My aunt says I can go to college,

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:36.820
but I think that would 
really be a drag on her.

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:43.750
So my third year of high school will 
be my last for rhythmic gymnastics.

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:46.960
I have only these three years.

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:49.860
That's why I have to make every day...

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:55.590
No, I have to make every hour, 
minute, and second count.

00:17:57.990 --> 00:17:59.970
Yeah... I feel the same!

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:05.850
I want to keep performing with you
 for the next three years.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:07.560
First, we're going to the Inter-High.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.820
All of us! Together!

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:14.330
Yeah.

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:24.290
Why'd you take Shotaro to Misato's house?

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:29.580
You three are graduating 
after this year's tournament.

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:33.760
Watari-kun and Asa-chan 
will be gone after next year, too.

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:39.460
That leaves Futaba-kun and Misato-kun

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:41.690
to define Ao High's MRG team.

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:53.940
<b>Drive\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hDedication\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hCourage!!</b>

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:06.370
Damn it!

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:08.540
Wait, did...

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:10.500
Did Misato just swear?

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.520
One more time, please!

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:18.090
I've never seen Misato-kun 
show this kind of emotion.

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:23.560
Misato-kun.

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:27.740
When I performed, I did things alone.

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:29.340
I was on a team...

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.580
Yet I didn't trust anyone. 
I performed by myself.

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:35.020
And in the end...

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:38.020
I destroyed myself and my team.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:41.650
But you're not like me.

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:44.580
You've made a choice 
to soar with the others.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:47.410
And they've chosen to soar with you.

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:51.660
Everyone here wants to soar together.

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:59.440
You've already surpassed me.

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:02.930
So don't worry. I know you can do this.

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:49.050
All right!

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:50.110
Misato-kun!

00:20:50.110 --> 00:20:54.220
I knew our Comeback Ace
 and Honest Leaf could do it!

00:20:58.490 --> 00:20:59.630
Coach!

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:03.390
Despite all that you said...

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:08.410
I really love your backflips!

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:16.790
<i>When I'm with Misato-kun and the team...</i>

00:21:17.490 --> 00:21:19.020
<i>I know I can soar.</i>

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:21.740
<i>I can soar higher!</i>
